config-connector-extensions patch 0057: mockgcp's policies.patch (Cloud
DNS) is a partial update.

DNSPolicyFields (dns.gcp.hfl.dev, docs/design.md decision 37) sets a DNS
server policy's dns64Config with policies.patch; Config Connector's
DNSPolicy (Terraform) patches the policy's other fields without it.
mockgcp's patch replaced the whole policy with the request, so either
write erased the other's fields. The API's patch "applies a partial
update": only the fields the request sets now change. Upstream
candidate: yes.

diff --git a/mockgcp/mockdns/policy.go b/mockgcp/mockdns/policy.go
index fe6c4c9..5421170 100644
--- a/mockgcp/mockdns/policy.go
+++ b/mockgcp/mockdns/policy.go
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ import (
 	"google.golang.org/grpc/codes"
 	"google.golang.org/grpc/status"
 	"google.golang.org/protobuf/proto"
+	"google.golang.org/protobuf/reflect/protoreflect"
 	"google.golang.org/protobuf/types/known/emptypb"
 	apierrors "k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/errors"
 
@@ -166,7 +167,15 @@ func (s *policiesService) PatchPolicy(ctx context.Context, req *pb.PatchPolicyRe
 		return nil, err
 	}
 
-	updated := proto.CloneOf(req.Policy)
+	// A partial update, as the API's patch: only the fields the request
+	// sets change, so a patch from a client that does not know a field
+	// (Terraform's DNSPolicy and dns64Config) leaves it alone
+	// (config-connector-extensions' DNSPolicyFields).
+	updated := proto.CloneOf(&existing)
+	req.GetPolicy().ProtoReflect().Range(func(fd protoreflect.FieldDescriptor, v protoreflect.Value) bool {
+		updated.ProtoReflect().Set(fd, v)
+		return true
+	})
 
 	updated.Id = existing.Id
 	updated.Kind = existing.Kind
